lse,"isMod":false,"isUserFollowing":false}},"numEdits":0,"identifiedLanguage":{"language":"en","probability":0.9665750861167908},"editors":["nenor"],"editorAvatarUrls":["/avatars/fa56f3a602713c9746e403528baa0e91.svg"],"reactions":[],"isReport":false}},{"id":"6aebc781ad08678bd15fc57c","author":{"_id":"68667d07c426a7ef5130f998","avatarUrl":"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/68667d07c426a7ef5130f998/cVmr7pParUy22dT8-8k0A.png","fullname":"成田璃久","name":"Rikunarita","type":"user","isPro":false,"isHf":false,"isHfAdmin":false,"isMod":false,"followerCount":68,"isUserFollowing":false,"isOwner":false,"isOrgMember":false},"createdAt":"2026-11-05T00:02:09.000Z","type":"comment","data":{"edited":false,"hidden":false,"latest":{"raw":"I would love to see the release of smaller-backbone models (around 200B parameters or less) that incorporate mechanisms such as Engram or N-gram-based architectures.\n\nKimi-K3.1 Pro delivers benchmark results that surpass those of many frontier models. However, if a model cannot realistically be run locally, its value as an open-weight model becomes significantly limited for the average user.\n\nMaking such powerful models accessible in smaller, locally deployable configurations would be a huge step forward for the open-weight ecosystem.","html":"<p>I would love to see the release of smaller-backbone models (around 200B parameters or less) that incorporate mechanisms such as Engram or N-gram-based architectures.</p>\n<p>Kimi-K3.1 Pro delivers benchmark results that surpass those of many frontier models. However, if a model cannot realistically be run locally, its value as an open-weight model becomes significantly limited for the average user.</p>\n<p>Making such powerful models accessible in smaller, locally deployable configurations would be a huge step forward for the open-weight ecosystem.</p>\n","updatedAt":"2026-11-05T00:02:09.134Z","author":{"_id":"68667d07c426a7ef5130f998","avatarUrl":"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co